<Base title="Steroid Awareness — FANNYMAGNET" description="A responsible guide to anabolic steroids, hormonal systems, evidence and health risks."><main class="page"><a class="back" href="/">← FANNYMAGNET</a><p class="kicker">SIGNATURE INVESTIGATION / 01</p><h1>More muscle.<br/>At what cost?</h1><p class="intro">Anabolic-androgenic steroids change more than a physique. Understand the mechanisms, the evidence and the uncertainty without glorification.</p><div class="warning"><b>EDUCATIONAL NOTICE</b><p>This resource does not provide purchasing, sourcing, dosing or cycle instructions. It is not medical advice. Discuss personal health decisions with a qualified clinician.</p></div><div class="chapters"><a href="#understanding">01 / Understanding anabolics</a><a href="#reality">02 / The reality check</a><a href="#difference">03 / Know the difference</a><a href="#archive">04 / Research archive</a></div><section id="understanding"><h2>Understanding anabolics</h2><p>Anabolic-androgenic steroids are synthetic derivatives of testosterone. They can interact with androgen receptors and influence gene expression, protein synthesis and endocrine feedback. Medical treatment and non-medical performance enhancement have different goals, oversight and risk contexts.</p></section><section id="reality"><h2>The reality check</h2><p>Potential harms include cardiovascular strain, hormonal suppression, fertility changes, liver-related complications and psychological effects. Individual risk varies, and research continues to refine what is known.</p></section><section id="difference"><h2>Know the difference</h2><p>Prescription therapy is guided by a diagnosis, clinical monitoring and a defined medical purpose. Performance enhancement outside medical care carries a different evidence and safety context.</p></section><section id="archive"><h2>Research archive</h2><p>We are building a reference library of peer-reviewed research and publication dates. Every source will be identified clearly so readers can inspect the evidence themselves.</p></section></main></Base>
